{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KuZM4N4gy24VtpGkH3gaVQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd103-pathchk\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/pathchk: Check Whether File Names Are Valid or Portable\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS does not ship pathchk. GNU pathchk validates pathnames against POSIX portability\n6\t  rules. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gpathchk,\n7\t  installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n8\t\n9\tgoals:\n10\t  - G1: Check pathnames for validity and POSIX portability.\n11\t  - G2: Support strict POSIX and extended portability checks.\n12\t  - G3: Verify functional parity against gpathchk via differential testing.\n13\t\n14\trequirements:\n15\t  R1:\n16\t    title: Pathname checking\n17\t    items:\n18\t      - R1.1:\n19\t          text: Must check each given pathname and print an error to stderr if the path is invalid on the current system (component too long, non-existent leading directory).\n20\t      - R1.2:\n21\t          text: \"-p or --portability must check each pathname against POSIX portability rules: only portable filename characters (A-Z, a-z, 0-9, ., _, -), component length at most 14 characters, total path length at most 256 characters.\"\n22\t      - R1.3:\n23\t          text: \"-P must check that the pathname does not contain a leading hyphen in any component.\"\n24\t      - R1.4:\n25\t          text: Must process multiple pathname arguments, checking each and printing errors for invalid ones.\n26\t\n27\t  R2:\n28\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n29\t    items:\n30\t      - R2.1:\n31\t          text: Must exit 0 when all pathnames pass validation.\n32\t      - R2.2:\n33\t          text: Must exit 1 when any pathname fails validation.\n34\t      - R2.3:\n35\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n36\t\n37\tnon_goals:\n38\t  - cmd/pathchk does not create or modify files.\n39\t\n40\tacceptance_criteria:\n41\t  - id: AC1\n42\t    criterion: \"pathchk validpath exits 0, matching gpathchk.\"\n43\t    traces:\n44\t      - R1.1\n45\t  - id: AC2\n46\t    criterion: \"pathchk -p 'invalid/path@name' exits 1 with error, matching gpathchk -p.\"\n47\t    traces:\n48\t      - R1.2\n49\t  - id: AC3\n50\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gpathchk passes.\"\n51\t    traces:\n52\t      - R1.1\n53\t      - R1.2\n54\t      - R1.3\n55\t  - id: AC4\n56\t    criterion: \"cmd/pathchk compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n57\t    traces:\n58\t      - R1.1\n59\t      - R1.2\n60\t      - R1.3\n61\t      - R1.4\n62\t      - R2.1\n63\t      - R2.2\n64\t      - R2.3\n65\t\n66\tpackage_contract:\n67\t  imports:\n68\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"96e60321-b696-4fc0-bad2-bb3f752ba841","uuid":"e3609354-4304-4da3-832d-088a466ffc2d","timestamp":"2026-05-27T15:20:41.138Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5596/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd103-pathchk.yaml","content":"id: srd103-pathchk\ntitle: \"cmd/pathchk: Check Whether File Names Are Valid or Portable\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS does not ship pathchk. GNU pathchk validates pathnames against POSIX portability\n  rules. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gpathchk,\n  installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Check pathnames for validity and POSIX portability.\n  - G2: Support strict POSIX and extended portability checks.\n  - G3: Verify functional parity against gpathchk via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Pathname checking\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must check each given pathname and print an error to stderr if the path is invalid on the current system (component too long, non-existent leading directory).\n      - R1.2:\n          text: \"-p or --portability must check each pathname against POSIX portability rules: only portable filename characters (A-Z, a-z, 0-9, ., _, -), component length at most 14 characters, total path length at most 256 characters.\"\n      - R1.3:\n          text: \"-P must check that the pathname does not contain a leading hyphen in any component.\"\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Must process multiple pathname arguments, checking each and printing errors for invalid ones.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when all pathnames pass validation.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any pathname fails validation.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/pathchk does not create or modify files.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"pathchk validpath exits 0, matching gpathchk.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"pathchk -p 'invalid/path@name' exits 1 with error, matching gpathchk -p.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gpathchk passes.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/pathchk compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n","numLines":69,"startLine":1,"totalLines":69}}}
