k mode, and orchestrating the main logic.\n\nI need to be careful about how empty names are reported across modes: the -P flag outputs \"empty file name\" without quotes, while default mode wraps it in single quotes. For the default mode specifically, I'm checking whether each existing path prefix is a directory and searchable, but non-existent prefixes don't cause errors—only existing ones that lack search permissions do.\n\nStill implementing the structure... Writing the pathchk implementation... Writing argument parser... Writing validation logic...\n\nNow I'm thinking through how the `-p` and `-P` flags interact when both are specified—they're independent checks that both run, so a path could fail one check but pass the other, and both violations would be reported.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3130,"cache_read_input_tokens":41880,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3130},"output_tokens":30,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"96e60321-b696-4fc0-bad2-bb3f752ba841","uuid":"f20aa4a8-9cd6-4670-891f-9c465eb7ad74"}
